/* Standard evolution recipes.

   Recipe is an authoring-time file grouping only. The executable declarations
   remain ordinary functions, and their bodies use the common call syntax. */

package std:grammaticalization:
    schema = conlang.functions/v1

/* Bleach a verb sense, reanalyse its syntactic category, then increase its
   entrenchment. Step 17 evaluates these calls as a sequential handoff.

   This is the parameterised path mechanism of P52: one function, not one per
   path. Which source concepts may travel to which target semantics, and how
   much entrenchment each move carries, live in data/paths.tsv. `delta` is an
   ordinary parameter here because the caller resolves it while the source
   concept is still readable — by the time `drift` has run, this sign's core
   gloss is the target, and the path row could no longer be found. */
function VerbToTense(verb [Verb], tense, result_category, delta):
    drift(verb, sense: core, gloss: tense)
    reanalyze(verb, target: category, to: result_category)
    entrench(verb, delta: delta)
